Building Tarantool on macOS
===========================

Tested on: macOS 15 Sequoia, arm64 (Apple M-series), Apple clang 21, CMake 4.x.
Should work on macOS 13+ with Homebrew. MacPorts instructions are in section 4.


1. Quick start (Homebrew)
--------------------------

Run the dependency installer from the repository root:

    # Build dependencies only:
    bash tools/install-deps-macosx.sh

    # Build + LLVM JIT support:
    bash tools/install-deps-macosx.sh --jit

    # Build + test harness dependencies:
    bash tools/install-deps-macosx.sh --test

    # Everything:
    bash tools/install-deps-macosx.sh --all

Then build:

    mkdir -p build && cd build
    cmake .. \
        -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
        -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$(brew --prefix openssl@3);$(brew --prefix readline);$(brew --prefix icu4c);$(brew --prefix libiconv);$(brew --prefix zlib)" \
        -DDARWIN_BUILD_TYPE=None \
        -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5
    make -j$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu) tarantool


2. Manual dependency installation (Homebrew)
---------------------------------------------

2.1 Build dependencies

    brew install cmake make openssl@3 readline icu4c libiconv zlib python3

2.2 LLVM (only needed for ENABLE_SQL_JIT or ENABLE_SQL_CNP)

    brew install llvm

    llvm is keg-only (not symlinked into /opt/homebrew). Pass the LLVM cmake
    directory explicitly; see section 3.3.

    Note: ENABLE_SQL_CNP disassembler support is wired for x86 only. On arm64
    LLVM is still required so cmake can find the package, but no x86 libraries
    are linked in.

2.3 Python packages (for the test harness)

    pip3 install pyyaml gevent python-daemon six msgpack tarantool

2.4 Git submodules

    git submodule update --init --recursive
    # test-run has its own nested submodules:
    git -C test-run submodule update --init

2.5 Git tag (required for cmake version detection)

    cmake reads `git describe --long HEAD` to set the build version. If the
    repository has no annotated tags (e.g. a private fork), this fails. Create
    a placeholder tag:

        git tag -a 2.11.0 -m "placeholder version tag" HEAD


3. CMake configuration
-----------------------

3.1 Basic debug build (interpreter only)

    mkdir -p build && cd build
    cmake .. \
        -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
        -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$(brew --prefix openssl@3);$(brew --prefix readline);$(brew --prefix icu4c);$(brew --prefix libiconv);$(brew --prefix zlib)" \
        -DDARWIN_BUILD_TYPE=None \
        -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5
    make -j$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu) tarantool

3.2 RelWithDebInfo build

    Replace -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug with -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo.

3.3 With LLVM JIT (ENABLE_SQL_JIT)

    cmake .. \
        -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo \
        -DENABLE_SQL_JIT=ON \
        -DLLVM_DIR=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/cmake/llvm \
        -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$(brew --prefix openssl@3);$(brew --prefix readline);$(brew --prefix icu4c);$(brew --prefix libiconv);$(brew --prefix zlib);$(brew --prefix llvm)" \
        -DDARWIN_BUILD_TYPE=None \
        -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5

3.4 With Copy-and-Patch JIT (ENABLE_SQL_CNP)

    ENABLE_SQL_CNP requires clang-19+ and is currently x86-only for stencil
    generation. On arm64 the flag can be set but no stencils are produced;
    LLVM is still required for the package to be found by cmake.

        cmake .. \
            -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
            -DENABLE_SQL_CNP=ON \
            -DLLVM_DIR=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/cmake/llvm \
            -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="..." \
            -DDARWIN_BUILD_TYPE=None \
            -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5

3.5 Why -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5

    The top-level CMakeLists.txt declares cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 2.8),
    which CMake 4.x rejects. This flag suppresses the error without modifying
    source files.

3.6 MacPorts

    Replace -DDARWIN_BUILD_TYPE=None with -DDARWIN_BUILD_TYPE=Ports.
    MacPorts installs into /opt/local; cmake will find headers and libraries
    there automatically.


4. Running the test suites
---------------------------

Always run suites sequentially — test-run workers share ports and temp dirs.

    BUILDDIR=/path/to/build  # absolute path required

    # sql suite
    python3 test/test-run.py --builddir $BUILDDIR --suite sql --force -j 1

    # sql-tap suite (exclude known pre-existing failures)
    python3 test/test-run.py --builddir $BUILDDIR --suite sql-tap --force -j 1 \
        --exclude default.test.lua \
        --exclude gh-2579-custom-aggregate.test.lua \
        --exclude gh-2723-concurrency.test.lua

    # sql-luatest suite
    python3 test/test-run.py --builddir $BUILDDIR --suite sql-luatest --force -j 1

Use --force -j 1 on macOS. Without --force, gevent workers stop on the first
failure, leaving the remaining tests unreported as "undone".

4.1 JIT / dispatcher test modes

Pass environment variables before python3:

    VDBE_DISPATCHER=generated python3 test/test-run.py ...   # generated interpreter
    SQL_JIT_ENABLE=1 VDBE_DISPATCHER=generated python3 ...  # LLVM MCJIT
    VDBE_DISPATCHER=cnp python3 test/test-run.py ...         # Copy-and-Patch JIT


5. Known issues on macOS
--------------------------

- Apple clang 21 (Xcode 26) is stricter than earlier versions. The source
  tree includes fixes for -Wgnu-alignof-expression, -Wvla-extension-static-
  assert, -Wunterminated-string-initialization, and -Wsometimes-uninitialized.

- CMake 4.x removes compatibility with cmake_minimum_required < 3.5. Use
  -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 as a workaround until the CMakeLists
  minimum version is bumped.

- expr(1) on macOS uses BSD syntax. The `expr match str pat` form (GNU-only)
  has been replaced with `expr "$str" : "pat"` in extra/mkopcodeh.sh.

- The ZLIB::ZLIB cmake target may be created twice (once by LLVMConfig.cmake,
  once by the project's own FindZLIB.cmake). cmake/FindZLIB.cmake guards
  against this with an if(TARGET) check.

-- EOF
